{{Quote|When someone comes from what's ours, they don't try it twice. We work an honest day and a long one. We're the good guys but you wouldn't want to meet us in the dark. Where I come from, when someone pushes you, you push back harder. Just like these dune worms are doing! You come at a farmboy, well... You reap what you sow.|[[Luke Skywalker]], to [[Sergeant]] [[Kreel]]|<ref name="Storms of Crait">[[The Last Jedi – The Storms of Crait 1|''The Last Jedi – The Storms of Crait'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:MattisFarm.png|thumb|right|200px|Farmer [[Mattis Banz]] on a [[hemmel reaper]]]]
'''Farmers''', also known as '''ranchers''' or '''farmhands''', were [[farm]] workers or owners. On [[desert]] [[Planet|worlds]] like [[Tatooine]], [[moisture farmer]]s harvested [[water]] from the [[atmosphere]].<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> During the [[Imperial Era]], farmers on [[Lothal]] were sometimes dispossessed of their land.<ref name="FF">{{Rebels|Fighter Flight}}</ref>

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[Luke Skywalker]] is described in the original [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'']] script as a "'''farm boy'''."<ref name="IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

